---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="SEO & AI Resources"
  description="Curated SEO and AI resources – blogs, newsletters, podcasts, and tools. The information diet that keeps Robert Lora current on search and AI."
  currentSlug="resources"
>
  <div class="note-content">
    <h1>🔖 resources</h1>

    <p>my information diet for staying current on AI and SEO.</p>

    <h2>seo blogs & publications</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://ahrefs.com/blog" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ahrefs blog</a> - data-driven SEO research. I use their API daily and built a 567-line validator to keep costs in check</li>
      <li><a href="https://searchengineland.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">search engine land</a> - where I first hear about most algorithm updates</li>
      <li><a href="https://searchenginejournal.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">search engine journal</a> - tactical how-to guides. less news, more "here's how to actually do it"</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.kevin-indig.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">kevin indig</a> - growth memo newsletter. consistently the best thinking on where SEO meets product</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>seo people</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/lilyraynyc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">lily ray</a> - the person I check first after every google update</li>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/gofishchris" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">chris long</a> - Go Fish Digital. sharp on technical SEO and link building at scale</li>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/5le" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">eli schwartz</a> - product-led SEO. asks "should this page exist at all" before "how do we rank it"</li>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/willcritchlow" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">will critchlow</a> - SEO testing and experimentation</li>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/aaborstings" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aleyda solís</a> - international SEO</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>ai people & channels</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/karpathy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">andrej karpathy</a> - makes neural networks make sense even if you don't write code. his "let's build GPT from scratch" video is the best intro to how LLMs work</li>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/emollick" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ethan mollick</a> - the rare academic who builds with the tools he studies. his AI usage frameworks actually hold up at work</li>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/swyx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">swyx (shawn wang)</a> - first to surface AI news that matters. runs the latent space podcast</li>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/bcherny" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">boris cherny</a> - claude code creator</li>
      <li><a href="https://x.com/trq212" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">thariq</a> - claude code team</li>
      <li><a href="https://elevenlabs.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">elevenlabs</a> - voice AI experimentation. consistently early on new model demos</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/@aiexplained-official" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Explained</a> - model breakdowns and news</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/@AIJasonZ" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI jason</a> - vibe coding and practical experiments</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">claude code releases</a> - changelog and updates</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>podcasts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.latent.space/podcast" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">latent space</a> - the AI engineer podcast (Swyx & Alessio). gets technical without losing the thread</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.nopriors.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">no priors</a> - AI, technology and startups (Elad Gil & Sarah Guo)</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.dwarkeshpatel.com/podcast" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">dwarkesh podcast</a> - deep dives with AI leaders</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>newsletters</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://simonwillison.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">simon willison</a> - one of the best at experimenting with LLMs in public. reads everything, tries everything, shares what he finds</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.eugeneyan.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">eugene yan</a> - RAG, evals, prompting strategies</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.bensbites.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ben's bites</a> - daily AI digest</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>tools I use daily</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://ahrefs.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ahrefs</a> - backlinks, keywords, competitive research</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.semrush.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">semrush</a> - AI topic research and content gap analysis</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.screamingfrog.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">screaming frog</a> - technical audits</li>
      <li><a href="https://search.google.com/search-console" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">google search console</a> - the actual source of truth for search performance</li>
      <li><a href="https://pitchbox.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pitchbox</a> - outreach at scale</li>
      <li><a href="https://claude.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">claude</a> - the AI I've built everything on this site with</li>
      <li><a href="https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">claude code</a> - the CLI where the <a href="/builds">45 builds</a> happened</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.firecrawl.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">firecrawl</a> - web scraping and site crawling</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Layout>
